---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Terms of use | Broken Records" description="Terms for using Broken Records, and how to request a takedown.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="doc">
      <h1>Terms of use</h1>
      <p class="muted">Last updated October 8, 2026</p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>Broken Records (brokenrecords.com) is a website about world records. It is a brand of Mohr Creative Group LLC, based in Tennessee. By using this site, you agree to these terms.</p>

      <h2>Using the site</h2>
      <p>You may read, share links to, and quote short passages from our pages for personal, non-commercial use, with a link back to the record. Please do not copy whole pages, republish our stories, or use our images without written permission.</p>

      <h2>Where the information comes from</h2>
      <p>Each record page lists its sources. We write our own summaries and check them against those sources, but records change. A record may have been broken, corrected, or annulled after we last checked it. Every record page shows the date we last checked it. Always confirm an important fact with the record body named on the page before you rely on it.</p>
      <p>Broken Records is not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by Guinness World Records or any other record-keeping organization. Names of organizations and products are used only to identify sources and facts. They remain the property of their owners.</p>

      <h2>Images and video</h2>
      <p>Some images and videos on this site are AI-generated illustrations. They are not photographs and do not show the people named in a record. Where we use a photograph, we credit the photographer and the license. We do not use AI-generated images to depict a real person as if they were a photograph of that person.</p>

      <h2>Takedown requests</h2>
      <p>If you own rights to content on this site, or if you are a person named on a record page and believe an image, quote, or statement about you is inaccurate, unfair, or should not appear, tell us. Email <a href="mailto:info@brokenrecords.com">info@brokenrecords.com</a> with:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your name and how to contact you</li>
        <li>The web address (URL) of the page or item</li>
        <li>What you want removed or corrected, and why</li>
        <li>Proof of your rights to the content, if you are a rights holder</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We review every request. If it is valid, we will remove or correct the content within 5 business days and tell you what we did. If we decide not to act, we will tell you why.</p>

      <h2>Accuracy</h2>
      <p>We work to keep records accurate, but we cannot promise that every fact is current or complete. We will correct errors when we learn of them. Use of this site is at your own risk.</p>

      <h2>Limits of liability</h2>
      <p>To the fullest extent the law allows, Broken Records and Mohr Creative Group LLC are not liable for any loss or damage that comes from using this site or relying on its content. This does not limit any right you have that cannot be waived by law.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update these terms. The date at the top shows when they last changed.</p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Tennessee, without regard to its conflict-of-law rules.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p><a href="mailto:info@brokenrecords.com">info@brokenrecords.com</a></p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .doc { max-width: 42rem; padding: 2.5rem 0 1rem; }
  .doc h1 { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
  .doc h2 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin: 1.8rem 0 0.4rem; }
  .doc p { margin: 0 0 0.8rem; }
  .doc ul { margin: 0 0 0.8rem; padding-left: 1.25rem; }
  .muted { color: var(--ink-soft); }
</style>
